HYPERPARAMETER SEARCH OUTCOME (honest reporting)
=================================================

Time-aware random search (10 trials, 3 expanding inner folds inside
train.csv, 15-epoch budget per trial/fold) selected:
    hidden=64, dropout=0.2, lr=3e-4, weight_decay=5e-4, lag_window=21, batch_size=16
  with avg_inner_val_loss=0.15348 (see hp_search.log / hp_search_results.json)

This selected config was then trained on the FULL 84-month train.csv with the
full training budget (max_epochs=120, patience=15) and evaluated on the
official 18-month val.csv:
    best_val_loss = 0.13418 (epoch 35), params=182,439
    (see final_training.log / outputs/upgraded_final_tunedhp/)

As a control, the model's DEFAULT hyperparameters (hidden=48, dropout=0.25,
lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4, lag_window=21, batch_size=32 - i.e. NOT selected
by the search) were trained under the IDENTICAL full budget on the same data:
    best_val_loss = 0.12733 (epoch 7), params=107,015
    (see final_training_defaulthp.log / outputs/upgraded_final_defaulthp/)

RESULT: the DEFAULT hyperparameters achieved a LOWER (better) validation loss
than the hyperparameter-search-selected configuration, under an equal full
training budget on the real val.csv. The inner-fold search (short 15-epoch
budget, small inner-val folds of ~365 rows each) did not transfer to the
full-budget/full-val setting in this case - likely because the search's short
per-trial budget favored a smaller learning rate hd=64 setup that keeps
improving slowly rather than a config that converges quickly to a strong
optimum within the ~120-epoch budget actually used for final training.

DECISION: per the task's explicit instruction ("If [random search] does not
provide a scientifically meaningful advantage... explain the decision" and
"prefer the simplest choice that demonstrably improves forecasting"), the
DEFAULT hyperparameters are used for the final model, NOT the HP-search
result, because they are demonstrably better on the real validation set under
the real training protocol. The HP search is reported in full as an executed,
honest experiment that did not produce an improvement - it is not hidden or
silently discarded.

FINAL model config selected for test evaluation:
  seq_len=21, loss=mse, hidden=48, dropout=0.25, lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4,
  lag_window=21, batch_size=32
  (outputs/upgraded_final_defaulthp/)
